WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.395 --> 00:00:08.236
- [Voiceover] I once saw
a high school teacher lead

00:00:08.236 --> 00:00:11.075
a simple, powerful
exercise to teach his class

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:13.299
about privilege and social mobility.

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:15.972
He started by giving each
student a scrap piece of paper

00:00:15.972 --> 00:00:17.642
and asked them to crumple it up.

00:00:18.003 --> 00:00:20.668
Then he moved the recycling
bin to the front of the room.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:23.141
He said, "The game is simple.

00:00:23.141 --> 00:00:25.443
"You all represent the
country's population,

00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:27.437
"and everyone in the country
has a chance to become

00:00:27.437 --> 00:00:30.220
"wealthy and move into the upper class.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:32.891
"To move into the upper
class, all you must do

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:34.811
"is throw your wadded-up
paper into the bin

00:00:34.811 --> 00:00:36.387
"while sitting in your seat."

00:00:36.387 --> 00:00:38.204
The students in the back
of the room immediately

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:40.812
piped up, saying, "This is unfair."

00:00:41.035 --> 00:00:43.045
They could see the rows of
students in front of them

00:00:43.045 --> 00:00:44.941
had a much better chance.

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:48.025
Everyone took their
shots and, as expected,

00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:51.417
most of the students in the
front made it, but not all,

00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.511
and only a few students in
the back of the room made it.

00:00:54.511 --> 00:00:56.873
He concluded by saying,
"The closer you were

00:00:56.873 --> 00:00:59.198
"to the recycling bin,
the better your odds.

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:01.398
"This is what privilege looks like.

00:01:01.398 --> 00:01:03.104
"Did you notice how the
only ones who complained

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:05.143
"about fairness were in
the back of the room?

00:01:05.143 --> 00:01:08.225
"By contrast, people in front
of the room were less likely

00:01:08.225 --> 00:01:10.686
"to be aware of the privilege
they were born into.

00:01:10.686 --> 00:01:14.387
"All they can see is 10 feet
between them and their goal.

00:01:14.745 --> 00:01:17.629
"Your job as students who
are receiving an education

00:01:17.629 --> 00:01:19.749
"is to be aware of your privilege,

00:01:19.749 --> 00:01:22.533
"and use this particular
privilege called education

00:01:22.533 --> 00:01:25.517
"to do your best to achieve
great things, all the while

00:01:25.517 --> 00:01:28.685
"advocating for those
in the rows behind you."

